{title: Take Your Delight}
{subtitle: Psalms 37:3–7}
{key: G}
{tempo: 77}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [G] | [G] | [Bm7] | [C] |
| [D#maj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I see the man whose way prospers, [Bm7]ev[C]ery scheme he makes goes [D#maj7]right
[G]And the anger starts to burn [Bm7]in me [C]and keeps me up at night [G]
But the song is singing soft[Bm7]ly, [C]do not burn and do [D#maj7]not [G]fret
Dwell in the land and do [Bm7]what's good, his word will hold [C]you [Cmaj7/B]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Am]Take your delight in the [D]LORD
And he will [G]give you what [D/F#]your heart [Em]asks [Em7/D]
[Am]Commit your way to the [D]LORD
Trust in [G]him, and he will [Em]act
Be [Am]still before the LORD and wait [D]patiently for him
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Like the morning breaking slow[Bm7]ly [C]over hills of grey and [D#maj7]blue
[G]He will bring your righteousness [Bm7]to light [C]and let it shine [G]for you
Like the noonday sun your jus[Bm7]tice [C]will be plain for all to [D#maj7]see
[G]So I lay my worry [Bm7]down and let him walk ahead of [C]me [Cmaj7/B]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [G] | [Bm7] | [C] | [D#maj7] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[G]Trust in the LORD and do good [Bm7]
[C]Dwell in the land and [D#maj7]make faithfulness your pasture [G]
Be still, be [C]still
Wait [D#maj7]patiently for him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Am]Take your delight in the [D]LORD
Trust in him, [G]and he will [Em]act
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Em] | [Am] | [D] | [G] [D/F#] |
| [Em7] | [Am] | [D] | [G] |
